      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I still haven't discovered where the issue is,but on the download speed slowdowns,It is not exactly the cdn at fault.I checked with wireshark and it seems the adapter is sending a TCP Zero Window message to the server which tells the server that the receiver buffer of the client is full so the server stops sending data until that buffer is cleared.There are many Dup Acks and TCP out of order too, and Interestingly,this happens even on the wifi ,but does not happen on my old H61 mobo with a i5 4400 whatsoever.Very strange.Not sure if this is related.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
