      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I have had this issue since I started with VRChat in early 2021, running the same motherboard the whole time (Gigabyte B550 Aorus Pro) and a 3080, upgrading the CPU once.\n\nHowever after upgrading my GPU to a 5090 and swapping out my PCI-E USB card just over a month ago, the problem seems to have completely disappeared. Before I usually had the issue after being in the same world for 2+ hours, now I've been as long as 7 hours in the same world without any issues.\n\nI updated to the latest graphics driver and the motherboard's BIOS got reset during the upgrade, but other than that I haven't changed anything that could be relevant. Still running the same BIOS as I updated to when I upgraded my CPU, and it would've been reset back then too.\n\nI haven't seen anyone else mention USB PCI-E cards and I'm not sure if that's relevant at all, but I went from an Inateck with 4 ports 1 controller, to a StarTech with 4 ports 4 controllers.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
